SUMMARY:[Grant Radar] ADMH Adolescent Early Intervention and/or Outpatient Substance Use Treatment Services – Region 4 — due
DESCRIPTION:A one-time pot of $250K x 2 for ADMH-certified providers to start adolescent SUD early intervention and outpatient care in Region 4. The RFP says ADMH wants awardees to 'adopt and integrate evidence-based treatment practices' and scores named EBPs\, so MORE training could be a budget line for a partner provider. Fit is weak because the population is adolescents.\n\nPath: Line-item · Priority 2.0\nhttps://mh.alabama.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/2027-09-Adolescent-Treatment.pdf
